WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.939
The world is about to plug back into the Matrix,
but will Laurence Fishburne be on the other

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.220
side this time around?

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.940
Warner Bros. dropped a bombshell on August
20 when it announced that filmmaker Lana Wachowski

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.100
- one half of the directorial duo behind the
original Matrix trilogy - is set to write

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.590
and direct the long-awaited fourth Matrix
film.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.410
Keanu Reeves will reprise his role as Neo,
and his co-star Carrie-Anne Moss is confirmed

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.560
to step back into her role as Nebuchadnezzar
crew member and Neo's love interest Trinity.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.520
That news break came as a welcome surprise,
and it seemed that The Matrix 4 would be one

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.260
big Matrix family reunion.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.120
The only problem?

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.980
There was no mention of Laurence Fishburne's
involvement in the film.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.600
Fishburne starred opposite Reeves and Moss
in all three Matrix movies, playing Morpheus,

00:00:40.609 --> 00:00:44.739
the Nebuchadnezzar captain who recruited Neo
to aid in the fight to break humanity free

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.020
from the virtual reality known as the Matrix.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.420
Considering Morpheus, Neo, and Trinity are
the core trio of the Matrix franchise, and

00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:55.399
given that Reeves and Moss are locked in for
The Matrix 4, you'd assume that Fishburne

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.300
would also come back for the upcoming film.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.280
However, that might not end up happening.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.580
According to Variety's Justin Kroll, Fishburne
may not return because the film might not

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.760
include his character at his current age.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.260
The Matrix 4 will reportedly feature a younger
version of Morpheus, and Warner Bros. is said

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.480
to be on the hunt for the perfect person for
the gig.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.480
Shortly after the initial news broke, Kroll
wrote on Twitter:

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.280
"If you've asked yourself, 'Where's [Morpheus],'
sources have told me this may point to where

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:24.000
and when the film is set as I've heard execs
are looking at a variety of actors to possibly

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.260
play 'young [Morpheus].'

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.520
Stay tuned on that front…"

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.600
Now, just because Warner Bros. is apparently
in an active search for the right person to

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:34.820
portray a fresh-faced version of everyone's
favorite freedom fighter doesn't completely

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.500
rule out the possibility that Fishburne will
appear in The Matrix 4.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.620
Someone new to the Matrix franchise might
step up and portray young Morpheus, with Fishburne

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:45.320
still appearing as the regular-aged version
of himself.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.100
Anything can happen in in the Matrix.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.140
Perhaps Warner Bros. knows exactly what it's
doing here, and is purposefully holding out

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.220
on announcing Fishburne's inclusion to build
additional buzz around the new Matrix.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.200
The studio already hit us with huge news when
it confirmed that the project was happening.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.220
Maybe Warner Bros. brass doesn't want to give
franchise fans everything all at once, and

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.720
is holding onto the juicy tidbit that is Fishburne's
potential involvement until a later date.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.740
"They are guarding all the doors, they are
holding all the keys, which means that sooner

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:14.300
or later someone is going to have to fight
them."

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.700
On that note, there's also the chance that
Warner Bros. is still negotiating with Fishburne

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.220
about returning as Morpheus.

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:24.340
It isn't every day that an actor learns that
the franchise they last appeared in 16 years

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:28.890
ago is getting another installment, and Fishburne
could very well be conflicted about the idea

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.379
of being a part of the new movie.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:35.599
He has remained incredibly busy in the time
since The Matrix Revolutions debuted in 2003

00:02:35.599 --> 00:02:40.099
- appearing in films like Mission: Impossible
III, Days of Wrath, Predators, Man of Steel,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:45.000
Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice, Ant-Man
and the Wasp, and two of the John Wick films.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.500
Fishburne has also found success on the small
screen in his post-Matrix life, playing Dr.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:54.650
Raymond Langston on a handful of CSI series,
Jack Crawford on Hannibal, and Earl "Pops"

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.460
Johnson on Black-ish and Grown-ish.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.520
Clearly, the guy has been doing pretty well
for himself over the years.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:03.680
This considered, it's plausible that Fishburne
is completely satisfied with his professional

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.200
life and may not be interested in reprising
his Matrix role that he hung up so many years

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.020
ago.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.120
It's a mystery for now whether Fishburne will
be involved in The Matrix 4, but for our part,

00:03:12.139 --> 00:03:16.169
we're holding out hope that we'll get to hear
him say a few iconic lines at least one more

00:03:16.169 --> 00:03:16.800
time.

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:19.760
"Free your mind."

